cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Antigravity_Codex_ClaudeCode_DeepSeekHarness: 面向科学计算与工程研发的四客户端配置与验证工具"
message: "If you use this software or workflow specification in academic research or engineering projects, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Xinyu
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xinyu-Li-1997/Antigravity_Codex_ClaudeCode_DeepSeekHarness"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24293507"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24293507
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Shared engineering rules (R0-R11) with client-idiomatic conditional filtering,
  a unified byte-stable single-entry lifecycle hook dispatcher (uguard_hook.py)
  that coexists cleanly with same-host native orchestration while hard-guarding
  workspace write boundaries, external headless dispatches, and completion bills,
  single-source hardened read-only review subagents, zero-blacklist lexical
  grounding and document hygiene checks, pre-read sizing and conservative
  sharding, cross-client coverage verification, deterministic mechanical
  reconciliation tables, read-only four-client capability evolution probes,
  on-demand academic writing guides (cae-writing), and an on-demand four-layer
  acyclic axiom verification machine (cae-axioms: dual-profile Python hard
  state machine, optional zero-Mathlib Lean 4 kernel audit, and clean-room
  packet replay) across Google Antigravity, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, and
  DeepSeek Harness for scientific computing, CAE, CFD, FEA, numerical PDE
  solvers, HPC, and high-reliability software engineering, implemented purely on
  the Python 3.11+ standard library across Windows, WSL2, and Linux.
keywords:
  - scientific-computing
  - computer-aided-engineering
  - computational-fluid-dynamics
  - finite-element-analysis
  - numerical-pde
  - coding-agents
  - verification-harness
  - deterministic-reconciliation
  - documentation-hygiene
  - formal-verification
  - lean4
  - axiom-verification
  - reproducible-workflows
